WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Kanagawa Junior 
Tennis Tournament Arena

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:04.740
Serve.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.360
Then I'll be on this side.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.750
Good luck.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.590
Good luck.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.540
Best-of-three-set match.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.180
Araya to serve.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:21.950
<i>Here I come!</i>

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:53.750
<i>I'm giving it everything from the start!</i>

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.530
What an amazing serve!

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:58.470
But it got returned!

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:01.720
<i>It's so heavy!</i>

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:11.190
<i>He has even more power than last year!</i>

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:13.540
Whoa, that was a great shot!

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.990
But Maruo managed to return it, too.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.610
All right!

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:28.750
Start with a Roar

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:31.520
All right!

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:34.750
Looks like it's started.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:35.680
Hello.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:36.510
Hey.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:37.730
He's so loud!

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:40.350
All he did was win a point on his serve.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:41.760
He's way too hyped up.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.410
<i>Araya-kun...</i>

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:46.450
Nice shot!

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.640
Araya-senpai, nice shot!

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:49.390
15-love.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:54.070
<i>His speed and the volume 
of his voice have increased,</i>

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:55.900
<i>yet he looks calm.</i>

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:05.430
Take Down Araya File
1. Aim for his weak point: his slow start.
2. Take your time during points and play at your own pace.
3. Contest of endurance.
4. It's important to concede points sometimes.
Especially with Araya-kun who has both speed and power on his side,
 it's normal to lose from time to time.
5. Avoid his fast-paced tempo and surprise him.

00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:02.340
<i>Item 1 of my Take Down Araya File from 
last year, his slow start, has been fixed!</i>

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.910
Fifteen seconds.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:08.150
<i>Fifteen seconds have passed.</i>

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.230
<i>Last year, he would've been annoyed</i>

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:21.680
Take Down Araya File
1. Aim for his weak point: his slow start.
2. Take your time during points and play at your own pace.
3. Contest of endurance.
4. It's important to concede points sometimes.
Especially with Araya-kun who has both speed and power on his side,
 it's normal to lose from time to time.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:17.770
<i>just by me fixing my strings.</i>

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:20.200
<i>But he's able to keep his concentration.</i>

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.730
<i>I should cross off everything else I can now,</i>

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:27.680
<i>early in my return game, while my risk factor is low.</i>

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.250
<i>Watch carefully</i>

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.220
<i>and apply it to last year's data!</i>

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:35.810
<i>Wide!</i>

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:40.070
30-love.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.030
Yes!

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:42.770
<i>That's right...</i>

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:44.890
<i>Araya-kun can change the course of his shots</i>

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:47.040
<i>just before contact, thanks to his strong wrists.</i>

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:55.170
Take Down Araya File
1. Aim for his weak point: his slow start.
2. Take your time during points and play at your own pace.
3. Contest of endurance.
4. It's important to concede points sometimes.
Especially with Araya-kun who has both speed and power on his side,
 it's normal to lose from time to time.
5. Avoid his fast-paced tempo and surprise him.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:49.860
<i>And his serves are powerful.</i>

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.990
<i>I'll have to give up on trying to get those aces.</i>

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:55.170
<i>But that doesn't mean I can stop collecting information.</i>

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.800
<i>I returned it somehow!</i>

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:04.400
<i>Last year I had to seize the initiative 
by force in my return game,</i>

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.800
<i>but it's different now.</i>

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:09.810
<i>I'm going to go for it and 
use my 1/81 control!</i>

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:14.290
Wow! What a spot to aim for!

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:15.770
And he moved up even closer!

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:17.750
<i>He's fast!</i>

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:18.900
<i>His counter's coming!</i>

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.240
<i>If I don't see his habit of 
dropping his shoulder...</i>

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:22.150
<i>It'll be straight!</i>

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:24.680
40-love.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:26.740
Yeah, bring it! Come on!

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:31.450
<i>He got me even though I used 
my low-risk 1/81 control.</i>

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:34.330
<i>To top it off, I even knew 
what direction it was going...</i>

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.330
<i>This is Araya-kun's counter.</i>

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.380
<i>The weapon of a player in Japan's top eight.</i>

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.830
<i>It's not enough for me just 
to hit a controlled shot.</i>

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:44.340
<i>I have to change up my timing,</i>

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.240
<i>or create an open court...</i>

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.490
<i>And I have to think about 
how and when to do it.</i>

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:55.480
<i>Also, Araya-kun is impatient, so he 
wasn't strong in contests of endurance.</i>

00:04:56.150 --> 00:05:00.110
<i>Maybe slowing the pace and just
sticking it out would be a viable tactic.</i>

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.860
<i>Drop the pace with a slice!</i>

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:12.340
<i>It's no good.</i>

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:15.320
<i>A slower pace and endurance 
alone won't win me points.</i>

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:17.580
<i>There's no other way but to be aggressive.</i>

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:22.340
<i>In that case, the last item of 
the Take Down Araya File...</i>

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:22.340
5. Avoid his fast-paced tempo and surprise him.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:27.220
<i>Do something unexpected to disrupt his tempo!</i>

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.330
That's a nice drop shot!

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:30.870
He's rushing in even closer!

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.310
Araya's fast, too!

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.520
Game: Araya. 1-0.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.520
Yeah!

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.780
H-His legs are intense...

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:49.480
<i>But if I can pull it off right, 
what I just did might be effective.</i>

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:57.410
<i>I knew it wouldn't be like last year...</i>

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:05.070
Take Down Araya File
1. Aim for his weak point: his slow start.
2. Take your time during points and play at your own pace.
3. Contest of endurance.
4. It's important to concede points sometimes.
Especially with Araya-kun who has both speed and power on his side,
 it's normal to lose from time to time.
5. Avoid his fast-paced tempo and surprise him.

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:00.310
<i>But I figured out which tactics I can still use,</i>

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:04.930
<i>as well as which ones I can't use anymore, and why.</i>

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:09.620
<i>In a return game, you can't do much 
other than inch closer like this.</i>

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:13.330
<i>I'll figure out as much as I can, 
and when the time comes,</i>

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.430
<i>I'll be happy if I can break 
once, preferably twice.</i>

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.020
Time.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:23.270
<i>I polished my serve so I can 
make use of my return game!</i>

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.200
15-love.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.200
Yes!

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.730
Whoa, that was amazing...

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:36.880
Wasn't that as fast as Araya's?

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.620
I don't know. It might've been faster.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:48.230
<i>So this is how you were able 
to score against Miyagawa.</i>

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:52.340
<i>But that just means if I can do 
something about this, I can win.</i>

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.180
<i>I'll go for the center with a spin!</i>

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:57.180
Out!

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.340
30-love.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:01.190
<i>He returned it with all he had...</i>

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.770
<i>Next will be a slice that bounces wide!</i>

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.400
40-love.

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:13.530
<i>He returned it with a power shot again, 
even though it blew his posture.</i>

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:15.670
<i>Just as I thought.</i>

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:19.110
<i>It's hard to hit it with that speed and spin,</i>

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:21.120
<i>but it's not something I can't return.</i>

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:24.700
<i>Is he trying to hit back all the different serves</i>

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:27.550
<i>so his body can learn the varied timing?</i>

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:31.650
<i>He's going for the break in a forceful
way that's nothing like mine.</i>

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:34.390
<i>But I won't let that happen!</i>

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:36.940
<i>I've gotten three points 
with different serves so far,</i>

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:40.020
<i>so here's one he hasn't 
seen yet: my center slice!</i>

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:43.430
Out!

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:45.400
Game: Maruo. 1-all.

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:46.490
<i>Yes!</i>

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:47.650
<i>First and foremost, hold serve.</i>

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.840
Maruo's doing pretty well, too.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:52.030
He was able to hold serve against Araya.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.030
<i>What a troublesome serve.</i>

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:58.530
<i>He's changing up the trajectory by
varying the serve type and power.</i>

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:01.550
<i>That speed is inconceivable 
with a body like his,</i>

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:03.040
<i>yet he's also balanced.</i>

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:07.340
<i>For now, I'll be prepared for 
a flat shot, his fastest.</i>

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:10.670
<i>Beyond that, all I can do is make my 
body itself learn the differences.</i>

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:12.170
<i>Jeez.</i>

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:14.180
<i>He's as good as a national player!</i>

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.690
<i>For someone who had no speed or power,</i>

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:22.280
<i>you sure got a lot stronger since last year!</i>

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:26.610
15-love.

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:29.630
<i>To think that even with your build,</i>

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.940
<i>you managed to get stronger 
with only ingenuity and strategy.</i>

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.240
<i>I don't want to accept that.</i>

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:37.120
<i>But the fact that you won your way here</i>

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.370
<i>is proof that it's true.</i>

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:39.550
Yes!

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:41.830
<i>But as you get better at tennis,</i>

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.830
<i>your physique becomes 
increasingly important.</i>

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.360
<i>I'll show you that truth,</i>

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:50.730
<i>and the difference between us that you
can't make up for, right here and now!</i>

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.390
Game: Araya. 2-1.

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.610
<i>It's my serve.</i>

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:02.390
<i>I have to be sure to hold!</i>

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:07.600
<i>His return made it through!</i>

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:10.360
<i>But if it's my serve,</i>

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:11.170
<i>I can do this!</i>

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.740
<i>His left shoulder dropped!</i>

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.070
<i>Counter to crosscourt!</i>

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:19.450
15-love.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:20.810
<i>Yes!</i>

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:23.380
<i>If it's my serve, I can return his counters, too.</i>

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:25.250
<i>I can be more than an even match!</i>

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.000
A-Amazing...

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:30.590
Bro is able to handle Araya's speed and power.

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:32.730
How is he doing that without making errors?

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:36.170
It's not as though he's winning 
because of his footwork.

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:39.200
But not only is he exceptionally 
good at analyzing a situation,

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:42.210
his body, though average, 
has been trained hard.

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:45.060
And adding his keen eyes to the formula,

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:47.940
that's how he's playing at 
the same level as Araya.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:51.480
30-love.

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:54.990
In his current state, he 
obviously can't win with power.

00:09:56.710 --> 00:10:01.070
But by using accurate control to hit 
courses that are tough to follow,

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:04.750
his offense can match the 
level of that power shot.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:06.740
That's the most solid proof that

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:13.610
he's getting closer to the ultimate ideal he held 
in the beginning: "if you can return all shots

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:17.010
with excellent control, theoretically, 
you will never lose."

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:21.420
Game: Maruo.

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:21.950
Yes!

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:22.760
2-all.

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:26.580
Which means he has a 
chance of winning, right?

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.930
Yeah. The real battle starts now.

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:32.270
It all depends on which one will break first.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:34.780
Araya
Maruo

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:45.530
Araya
Maruo

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:49.890
Both of them want to break, but neither 
seems to be getting an opening.

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:56.110
Maruo-kun is aware of Araya-kun's 
tendency to play at a fast tempo,

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:58.720
so he's going for the break by using his control.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:00.510
On the other side,

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:04.510
Araya-kun is going for the break with 
his overwhelming power and speed.

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:07.620
They're both looking for a chance 
to deal a decisive blow.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.110
<i>But...</i>

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:12.520
<i>The way this is going might 
be a little problematic.</i>

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:16.240
Yes!

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:18.290
Game: Araya. 4-3.

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:22.050
<i>What is this awkward feeling?</i>

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.160
<i>Don't tell me he...</i>

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:34.920
<i>I'm holding serve, but I'm 
losing ground on this point.</i>

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:38.080
<i>But we should be playing at the same level.</i>

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:39.420
<i>So why?</i>

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:42.590
<i>I haven't been able to win on crucial points.</i>

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:45.210
<i>Is the reason I can't score points in the end</i>

00:11:45.210 --> 00:11:47.430
<i>just because I'm unlucky?</i>

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:51.650
<i>It'd be great if I could learn something 
from looking over my old data,</i>

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:54.040
<i>but court change is only a minute and a half...</i>

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:56.440
<i>Actually...</i>

00:11:56.440 --> 00:12:02.440
The beginning of his attacks: crosscourt
When Araya-kun plans his attack, he always begins with a crosscourt shot at a sharp angle to move me outside.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:12:02.440
When he does, he leans forward
slightly just before impact.

00:11:56.850 --> 00:12:02.440
<i>Araya-kun fixed his habit from last year 
of leaning forward after hitting crosscourt.</i>

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:06.700
<i>This couldn't be related to that, could it?</i>

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:11.690
Hey, Yukichi.

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:14.120
When Maruo lost to Araya last year,

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:16.870
did he say anything that stood out?

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:17.460
Huh?

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:22.040
I think he just said he didn't have 
the skill to beat him, or something.

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:24.470
Is something on your mind?

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:28.520
I almost forgot. He hasn't been 
playing tennis for that long.

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:30.660
So maybe he doesn't know

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:33.140
that Araya is left-handed.

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:36.450
What does it mean if your 
opponent is left-handed?

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:42.130
Simply put, a left-handed player 
has the upper hand in tennis.

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:43.790
What? Why?

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:47.420
The main reason is that there 
are fewer left-handed players.

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:52.000
That means right-handed players don't get 
many opportunities to play against them.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.960
But when Bro played against Araya last year,

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:57.520
he didn't mention having trouble with that.

00:12:57.520 --> 00:13:00.630
Then maybe he lost before he could realize it.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:04.100
Especially since there was such a 
huge difference in their skill levels.

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:04.970
I see.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.610
But it's different now.

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:09.560
Their skill levels are so evenly matched,

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:12.670
the smallest difference between the 
two will greatly impact the match.

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:14.730
Especially if the game gets drawn out.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:18.610
He's analytical, so I'm sure he'll notice,

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:20.610
but it's something that can't be helped.

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:23.000
<i>Huh?</i>

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:24.110
<i>Wait a second...</i>

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:26.540
<i>Here, here, and here...</i>

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:29.800
<i>Araya-kun's crosscourt 
forehand won points off me.</i>

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:34.020
Weaker     Araya     Forced into missing     Araya

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:34.020
Down the Line

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:34.020
Couldn't make it                                Crosscourt forehand

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:33.560
<i>His forehand crosscourt cornered my backhand...</i>

00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:36.260
<i>If the opponent isn't left-handed,</i>

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:39.250
<i>I wouldn't be able to return a crosscourt 
forehand with my backhand.</i>

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:41.210
<i>If that's the case...</i>

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.410
<i>The awkward feeling I had earlier was because</i>

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:44.760
<i>Araya-kun is left-handed?</i>

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:50.330
<i>But are left-handed forehands and 
right-handed backhands that different?</i>

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:53.980
<i>I feel like the trajectory is pretty similar...</i>

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:56.620
<i>Are Araya-kun's forehands special?</i>

00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:57.310
Time!

00:13:58.550 --> 00:14:00.800
<i>Since I couldn't find a clear answer,</i>

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.280
<i>I'll just have to figure it out as I play.</i>

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:05.830
<i>I'll find out what makes a 
left-handed forehand unique</i>

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:08.530
<i>during my serve, when I have the upper hand.</i>

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:13.290
<i>Remember to keep an eye out 
for his crosscourt forehand...</i>

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:22.390
Love-15.

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:26.010
<i>Looks like it's no mistake.</i>

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:27.210
<i>He's really</i>

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:30.550
<i>having trouble dealing with 
the fact that I'm left-handed.</i>

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:37.490
<i>A right-handed backhand and a left-handed 
forehand are indeed different.</i>

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:39.810
<i>But how are they different?</i>

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:46.170
Left Forehand

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:46.170
Point of contact is further
back for left forehand

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:42.460
<i>The point of contact? Follow-through?</i>

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:44.370
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:46.100
<i>Forehands and backhands are two</i>

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:47.890
<i>totally different shots to begin with.</i>

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:52.320
Left Forehand

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:52.320
Left forehands are further 
away from the center of gravity

00:14:47.890 --> 00:14:50.610
<i>That awkward feeling earlier was because I tried</i>

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:52.320
<i>to hit both back in the same way.</i>

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:54.690
<i>If that's the case, then what do I do?</i>

00:14:54.690 --> 00:14:56.070
Fifteen seconds.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:58.840
<i>Okay, for now...</i>

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:01.730
<i>To get used to left-handed shots 
in an efficient manner,</i>

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.980
<i>I'll watch Araya-kun's moves carefully...</i>

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:10.630
<i>And imagine how he looks when 
he turns just before he shoots.</i>

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:15.180
<i>Araya-kun is moving up!</i>

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:20.600
Love-30.

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:22.850
Yeah!

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:25.460
Araya, the baseliner, moved up!

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:27.430
He's finally going for it!

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:29.170
Two more points and he'll break!

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:29.940
Maruo!

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:31.240
Keep your eyes peeled!

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:32.830
<i>Damn...</i>

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:35.100
<i>Focusing like that narrowed 
my field of vision,</i>

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:36.740
<i>and I couldn't follow his moves.</i>

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:38.590
<i>That's right.</i>

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:40.000
<i>It's at times like these</i>

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:42.990
<i>that I have to widen my field of vision</i>

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:45.000
<i>and look at both the whole 
court and Araya-kun.</i>

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:47.250
<i>Don't overthink it...</i>

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:54.460
<i>Don't get stuck on just 
"right-handed" and "left-handed."</i>

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:57.140
<i>Just hit the way my instincts tell me to!</i>

00:15:59.060 --> 00:15:59.890
Out.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:00.990
Love-40.

00:16:00.990 --> 00:16:02.890
Maruo missed again!

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:05.190
Now Araya's got break point!

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:08.010
Wh-What's wrong, Maruo-kun.?

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:10.450
This seriously looks bad.

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:12.420
<i>This isn't good.</i>

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:15.200
<i>Trusting your instincts 
now isn't going to work.</i>

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:17.000
<i>Much like you,</i>

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:20.120
<i>your instincts don't know how to deal 
with a left-handed player, either.</i>

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:23.330
<i>If you overwhelm your pure 
instincts and end up missing,</i>

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:26.840
<i>it might accidentally lead to insecurity.</i>

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.170
<i>It's going to be rough if that happens.</i>

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:35.640
Out.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:38.680
Game: Araya. Score: 5-3.

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:39.590
Araya leads.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:42.430
Yeah, bring it!

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:44.870
Araya broke serve!

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:46.810
They're not on even footing anymore!

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:47.580
Maruo!

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:49.360
This isn't like you! Get it together!

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:50.610
Yes!

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:51.690
Araya-senpai!

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:53.360
Let's win this set!

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:56.310
<i>Th-That was weird just now.</i>

00:16:56.310 --> 00:16:58.830
<i>It's not just that he's left-handed.</i>

00:16:59.770 --> 00:17:01.830
<i>Something's weird about my shots, too!</i>

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:03.710
Araya
Maruo

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:03.710
Araya!

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:05.960
If you win this, you've got the first set!

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:07.080
It's just one break!

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:09.050
Hang in there, Maruo!

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:13.380
<i>My backhand is off now.</i>

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:16.370
<i>When I think about fixing it, 
it narrows my field of vision.</i>

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:20.140
<i>But letting my instincts take 
over isn't working, either.</i>

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:22.100
<i>Is there any data that can
help at a time like this?</i>

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:23.970
<i>That's right...</i>

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:27.130
<i>I don't have any data on left-handed 
players to begin with!</i>

00:17:28.260 --> 00:17:32.840
<i>Playing instinctively only worked when 
I had plenty of experience or data.</i>

00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:37.110
<i>There's no way my instincts can understand 
something my reason doesn't understand.</i>

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:37.110
Reason

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:37.110
Instinct

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:40.760
<i>Being left-handed is a weapon in itself.</i>

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:46.120
<i>Just like Takuma-san's height, 
Araya-kun's entire body is ideal for tennis.</i>

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:51.380
<i>First, I have to do something 
about this awkward sensation</i>

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:53.130
<i>and the poor condition my backhand is in.</i>

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:56.600
15-love.

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:01.000
H-He got an ace!

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.260
He's gunning to take the set!

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:07.530
<i>A wide slice!</i>

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:10.930
30-love.

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:13.210
<i>I see...</i>

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:14.470
<i>Until now, I've thought of</i>

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:17.250
<i>his serves as just mirror 
images of right-handed serves.</i>

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:18.500
<i>But a serve is where the</i>

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:21.030
<i>difference between right-handed 
and left-handed is most apparent!</i>

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:25.030
<i>In particular, that wide slice 
pushed me to the edge of the court</i>

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:27.040
Goes further out than                                             Spin direction is 
a right-handed serve.                              opposite of right-handed.

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:27.040
Ad court                   Wide slice

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:27.040
Backhand contact doesn't
reach as far as forehand

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:27.040
<i>and forced me to use my backhand.</i>

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:30.430
<i>Just when my backhand is 
being uncooperative as it is...</i>

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:35.120
<i>Backhand again!</i>

00:18:37.020 --> 00:18:39.090
Out. 40-love.

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.210
<i>He's definitely aiming for it.</i>

00:18:42.110 --> 00:18:45.970
<i>No hard feelings, but I'll be taking 
full advantage of your weaknesses.</i>

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:47.390
Here it comes!

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:48.900
Araya's set point!

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:51.060
Araya-san! Finish this in one shot!

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:53.310
Maruo-kun, you can do it!

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:56.590
<i>Calm down! Calm down!</i>

00:18:56.590 --> 00:19:00.120
<i>I feel like he's going to 
take it all if he scores now!</i>

00:18:56.590 --> 00:19:01.950
Scratch, scratch, scratch, scratch

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.950
<i>I have to organize my thoughts.</i>

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:10.770
Araya            Araya

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:10.770
Serve Cross-Forehand

00:19:02.630 --> 00:19:06.210
<i>The problem is Araya-kun's left-handed shots.</i>

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:08.130
<i>Especially his serves and crosscourt forehands</i>

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:10.440
<i>that bounce outwards as if there's a spin on them.</i>

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:15.210
Typically Advantageous
The closer the point of contact is to the center of gravity,
the more centrifugal force is gained along with power.

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:15.210
The closer the point of contact is to the center of gravity, 
the less centrifugal force.
Backhand
Because the point of contact isn't forced back, there is less power.

00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:12.460
<i>And the physical factor</i>

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:15.210
<i>is that I can't return those with my backhand.</i>

00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:17.690
<i>But that's not the only reason.</i>

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:20.290
<i>Ever since I made an error playing instinctively,</i>

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:22.620
<i>I'm no longer confident in my backhand.</i>

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:24.720
<i>That's my psychological factor.</i>

00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:27.990
<i>Physical and psychological factors...</i>

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:30.280
<i>Can I solve both at the same time?</i>

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:33.010
<i>If I can't, then which do I prioritize?</i>

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:35.820
<i>I have to be as efficient as possible.</i>

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.520
<i>This is the critical moment.</i>

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:40.240
Fifteen seconds.

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:42.490
<i>That's right!</i>

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:46.370
<i>I was never the type that could 
be confident with no basis for it.</i>

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:49.950
<i>If I can't figure out how to 
deal with the physical factor,</i>

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:53.630
<i>there's no way I can have confidence, 
my psychological factor.</i>

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:55.380
<i>Think!</i>

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:58.680
<i>His serve should come to my backhand again.</i>

00:19:58.680 --> 00:20:02.670
<i>Analyze the differences from a 
right-handed serve as much as possible...</i>

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:05.090
<i>Have my body learn them as I carefully adjust</i>

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:06.330
<i>the predicted point of contact.</i>

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:10.080
<i>How much will a left-handed serve 
bounce to my backhand?</i>

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:12.140
<i>Wide slice!</i>

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:15.580
<i>First, take one step toward the outside.</i>

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:17.670
<i>Imagine three ball widths 
ahead of where it is!</i>

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:19.290
<i>It's still not enough!</i>

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:20.280
<i>But I returned it!</i>

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:22.280
<i>I'm ready for the left forehand!</i>

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:29.410
Left Forehand

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:29.410
Left Forehand

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:26.510
<i>A left forehand can hit a ball 
farther than a right backhand.</i>

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:29.410
<i>Imagine the point of contact being 
slightly closer than it actually is.</i>

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:31.570
<i>Faster than usual by a beat!</i>

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:35.690
<i>I aimed for deep right, 
but it landed in the middle!</i>

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:37.000
<i>I'm still swinging too slowly.</i>

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:41.320
<i>It feels less awkward to 
return the left backhand.</i>

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:43.720
<i>The problem really is the left forehand!</i>

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:45.010
<i>Here it is!</i>

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:46.010
<i>Faster...</i>

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:48.100
<i>Yes!</i>

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:57.520
<i>That pattern just now...</i>

00:20:55.730 --> 00:21:01.990
Weaker                        Araya

00:20:55.730 --> 00:21:01.990
Down the line

00:20:55.730 --> 00:21:01.990
Couldn't make it.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:00.050
<i>When he's been nailing me with aces all this time,</i>

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:01.990
<i>a straight shot after the crosscourt forehand!</i>

00:21:02.270 --> 00:21:06.530
First set winner: Araya. Score: 6-3.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.830
Araya won the first set!

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:12.350
As expected, Araya's just a cut above.

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:14.960
I thought Maruo would put up a good fight.

00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:16.880
<i>He got me.</i>

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:20.710
<i>But at this point, I still have
time to adjust the issues.</i>

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:23.170
Araya
Maruo

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:23.170
<i>I'll do something about it, no matter what!</i>

00:21:26.070 --> 00:21:30.930
Left Forehand    Left Forehand    Right Backhand    Right Backhand
Strong                 Strong                    Weak                      Weak

00:21:26.070 --> 00:21:30.930
Strong                 Weak                    Strong                      Weak
Right Forehand   Right Backhand   Right Forehand    Right Backhand

00:21:26.070 --> 00:21:30.930
Left forehand is not only strong, 
but also lack experience handling it with right backhand.
Right Forehand is powerful, but can be handled with left backhand.
Both weak, balances out.

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:30.930
<i>This is why that left crosscourt forehand got me.</i>

00:21:31.170 --> 00:21:33.890
<i>I was able to return it after 
I finally figured it out.</i>

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:35.390
<i>As proof...</i>

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:37.890
<i>I was a step away from being 
able to return that straight shot</i>

00:21:37.890 --> 00:21:39.940
<i>when he'd been hitting aces the whole time.</i>

00:21:40.550 --> 00:21:43.120
<i>I was able to get that far during a return game.</i>

00:21:43.120 --> 00:21:45.160
<i>I'll be able to hold my next serve!</i>

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:48.970
<i>I was able to prevent 
myself from getting worse!</i>

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:55.680
<i>I don't understand.</i>

00:21:56.180 --> 00:21:59.460
<i>This is the final round of the 
high-level Kanagawa tournament.</i>

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:01.320
<i>Why would someone who made it this far</i>

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:04.080
<i>be so stymied by a left-handed player?</i>

00:22:05.190 --> 00:22:06.120
<i>No...</i>

00:22:06.120 --> 00:22:07.630
<i>He was like that, too.</i>

00:22:10.020 --> 00:22:11.080
Pardon me.

00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:13.970
How many points are needed to win a tiebreaker?

00:22:13.970 --> 00:22:16.120
Huh? You don't know?

00:22:16.120 --> 00:22:17.980
It's my first time having one in a match.

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:21.480
<i>An unbalance caused by a surge in growth.</i>

00:22:21.890 --> 00:22:23.880
<i>Although it's not as much as Ike,</i>

00:22:23.880 --> 00:22:26.990
<i>I can't underestimate your speed of growth.</i>

00:22:28.170 --> 00:22:30.970
<i>I'll have to do something about 
that as soon as possible.</i>

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
Next Time

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:03.920
For now, I've figured out how to 
deal with a left-handed player.

00:24:03.920 --> 00:24:05.750
In my current state, 
this is the best I can do.

00:24:06.170 --> 00:24:07.380
But if I can get the upper hand,

00:24:07.730 --> 00:24:09.380
I'll have more options to attack.

00:24:09.740 --> 00:24:11.510
All right, here I go!

00:24:11.510 --> 00:24:12.680
Araya 2 - 4 Maruo

00:24:11.890 --> 00:24:14.160
He was so baffled by dealing 
with a left-handed player,

00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:13.930
Araya 2 - 5 Maruo

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:15.340
Araya 3 - 5 Maruo

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:15.340
and he's come this far already?

00:24:15.340 --> 00:24:16.600
That's fine.

00:24:16.600 --> 00:24:20.150
I'm already used to petty tricks like that!

00:24:20.150 --> 00:24:22.020
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.020
Choices and Explosive Power

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:24.020
"Choices and Explosive Power."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:30.350
End
